\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

\looseness=-1
Across six benchmarks, 17.9--31.3\% of items exhibit temporal DIF while rankings remain stable ($\rho \geq 0.994$); base-vs-instruct reversals and web-overlap independence confirm signal beyond contamination, while cross-subject matching ($\Delta\mathrm{FPR}{=}0$), DEFF correction, and a Monitor/Triage/Correct protocol provide practical tools for ongoing psychometric auditing.

